> Just rebased to handle the latest change on luminance properly. I think the issue with retro compatibility can be avoided by keeping getter for `use_vr` temporarly if you want to have this merged before 4.0 release.

That could work, do we have a way to mark properties as deprecated? That would be pretty neat.
In this case we don't store the value on the viewport.
The getter of `use_xr` would simply return `viewport_mode != VIEWPORT_MODE_XR`
The setter of `use_xr` would simply be:
```
if (p_use_xr && viewport_mode != VIEWPORT_MODE_XR) {
  set_viewport_mode(VIEWPORT_MODE_XR);
} else if (!p_use_xr && viewport_mode == VIEWPORT_MODE_XR) {
  set_viewport_mode(VIEWPORT_MODE_2D_AND_3D);
}
```
This should ensure that even with saving both `use_xr` and `viewport_mode`, the correct mode would be restored on load even if `viewport_mode` is set to `VIEWPORT_MODE_3D`.

Then in a couple of builds we can retire `use_xr` as both properties will be saved when people are already using the new version. Maybe keep it in 4.0 and retire it in 4.0.1?

